  "id": "UC-049",
  "slug": "keep-proofs-in-use-cases",
  "name": "Keep proofs as regression tests",
  "description": "A proof that passed belongs to its use case, stored in the use case's file with its id, the intent and proposal it came from, its model, subject and check. prove(proposal) runs the proposal's pending proofs and the proofs of every use case except the ones the proposal supersedes, so a change that breaks any use case fails as a regression, on a touched use case or not; a superseded proof that still passes is noted, since the behavior may not have changed; failures go back to the implementer through feedback. lastro regress runs every use case's proofs alone, for example in CI. A use case with no proofs yet is reported as unproved rather than failing.",
